<title>FINLAND: AHLSTROM WINS FIM 300 MLN ORDER FROM M-BOTNIA -STT.</title>
<headline>AHLSTROM WINS FIM 300 MLN ORDER FROM M-BOTNIA -STT.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish engineering group A.Ahlstrom Oy won a 300 million order from pulp producer Metsa-Botnia Oy for an evaporation and soda recovery boiler plant, Finnish news agency STT reported on Monday.  </p>
<p>The facility would be delivered to Metsa-Botnia's Joutseno Pulp mill, Ahlstrom said in a statement.</p>
<p>The delivery is part of an expansion project at Joutseno Pulp, which will increase the mill's annual pulp production capacity to 410,000 tonnes per year by the end of 1998.</p>
<p>Metsa-Botnia is owned by Metsa-Serla Oy and UPM-Kymmene Oy .</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, news@reuters.fi</p>
